1
00:04:06,666 --> 00:04:12,666
The magic didn't end at midnight.

2
00:08:13,333 --> 00:08:19,333
Cinderella II: Dreams Come True is a family, animation,
romance film directed by John Kafka.

3
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:26,000
As a newly crowned princess, Cinderella quickly learns that life at the Palace - and
her royal responsibilities - are more challenging than she had imagined.

4
00:16:26,666 --> 00:16:32,666
In three heartwarming tales, Cinderella calls on her animal friends and her Fairy Godmother to help as she brings her own grace and
charm to her regal role and discovers that being true to yourself is the best way to make your dreams come true.

5
00:20:33,333 --> 00:20:39,333
Cinderella (voice), played by Jennifer Hale.

6
00:24:40,000 --> 00:24:46,000
Jaq / The Baker / Sir Hugh / Grand Duke / Bert / Flower
Vendor (voice), played by Rob Paulsen.

7
00:28:46,666 --> 00:28:52,666
Gus / Mert / Stable Hand (voice), played by Corey Burton.

8
00:32:53,333 --> 00:32:59,333
The King (voice), played by Andre Stojka.

9
00:37:00,000 --> 00:37:06,000
Fairy Godmother / Mary Mouse / Beatrice / Daphne / Drizella /
Countess Le Grande (voice), played by Russi Taylor.

10
00:41:06,666 --> 00:41:12,666
Lady Tremaine (voice), played by Susanne Blakeslee.

11
00:45:13,333 --> 00:45:19,333
Cinderella II: Dreams Come True (also known as Cinderella 2: Dreams Come True) is a 2002 American animated
direct-to-video fantasy anthology film and serves as the sequel to the 1950 film Cinderella.

12
00:49:20,000 --> 00:49:26,000
Directed by John Kafka from a screenplay written by Jill E.

13
00:53:26,666 --> 00:53:32,666
Blotevogel, Tom Rogers, and Julie Selbo, it is the first in the Cinderella franchise to use digital ink and
paint and stars the voices of Jennifer Hale, Russi Taylor, Corey Burton, and Rob Paulsen.

14
00:57:33,333 --> 00:57:39,333
The film centers on Jaq, Gus, the Fairy Godmother, and the rest of the mice, as they create a three-story narrative about what happened after
Cinderella married Prince Charming and moved in his castle along with the mice, her stepsisters, and Lady Tremaine's cat, Lucifer.

15
01:01:40,000 --> 01:01:46,000
Cinderella II: Dreams Come True was released on February 26, 2002, and received
generally negative reviews from critics, though it recouped its budget.

16
01:05:46,666 --> 01:05:52,666
The film explores themes of princess, magic, fairy, cartoon, musical.

17
01:09:53,333 --> 01:09:59,333
The tone is uplifting and emotional.
